##  Analysis and Insights

Full SQL is in [`pizza_sales_analysis.sql`](pizza_sales_analysis.sql).

### Q1. Total orders placed
```sql
SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT order_id) AS total_orders FROM orders;
```
**21,350 orders.** Together they contain 48,620 order lines and 49,574 pizzas.

### Q2. Total revenue
```sql
SELECT ROUND(SUM(p.price * od.quantity), 2) AS total_revenue
FROM order_details od JOIN pizzas p ON p.pizza_id = od.pizza_id;
```
**$817,860.05**. Average order value is about $38.31, with 2.32 pizzas per order.

### Q3. Highest-priced pizza
```sql
SELECT pt.name, p.size, p.price
FROM pizzas p JOIN pizza_types pt ON pt.pizza_type_id = p.pizza_type_id
ORDER BY p.price DESC LIMIT 1;
```
**The Greek Pizza (XXL), $35.95.** The next highest are Greek XL ($25.50) and Brie Carre S ($23.65).

### Q4. Most common pizza size ordered
```sql
SELECT p.size, SUM(od.quantity) AS total_quantity
FROM order_details od JOIN pizzas p ON p.pizza_id = od.pizza_id
GROUP BY p.size ORDER BY total_quantity DESC;
```
| Size | Pizzas sold | Share |
|---|---|---|
| **L** | 18,956 | 38.2% |
| M | 15,635 | 31.5% |
| S | 14,403 | 29.1% |
| XL | 552 | 1.1% |
| XXL | 28 | 0.06% |

![size](charts/size.png)

### Q5. Top 5 most ordered pizza types
```sql
SELECT pt.name, SUM(od.quantity) AS total_quantity
FROM order_details od
JOIN pizzas p ON p.pizza_id = od.pizza_id
JOIN pizza_types pt ON pt.pizza_type_id = p.pizza_type_id
GROUP BY pt.name ORDER BY total_quantity DESC LIMIT 5;
```
| Rank | Pizza | Quantity |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | The Classic Deluxe Pizza | 2,453 |
| 2 | The Barbecue Chicken Pizza | 2,432 |
| 3 | The Hawaiian Pizza | 2,422 |
| 4 | The Pepperoni Pizza | 2,418 |
| 5 | The Thai Chicken Pizza | 2,371 |

The top 5 are separated by only 82 pizzas, so no single pizza dominates.

![top5](charts/top5.png)

### Q6. Quantity ordered per category
```sql
SELECT pt.category, SUM(od.quantity) AS total_quantity
FROM pizza_types pt
JOIN pizzas p ON p.pizza_type_id = pt.pizza_type_id
JOIN order_details od ON od.pizza_id = p.pizza_id
GROUP BY pt.category ORDER BY total_quantity DESC;
```
| Category | Quantity | Share |
|---|---|---|
| Classic | 14,888 | 30.0% |
| Supreme | 11,987 | 24.2% |
| Veggie | 11,649 | 23.5% |
| Chicken | 11,050 | 22.3% |

![category](charts/category.png)

### Q7. Orders by hour of day
```sql
SELECT HOUR(`time`) AS hour_of_day, COUNT(*) AS total_orders
FROM orders GROUP BY HOUR(`time`) ORDER BY hour_of_day;
```
Two clear peaks: **lunch (12:00 to 13:59)** with 4,975 orders, and **dinner (17:00 to 18:59)** with 4,735 orders. Almost nothing happens before 11:00 or after 22:00.

![hour](charts/orders_by_hour.png)

### Q8. Category-wise distribution of the menu
```sql
SELECT category, COUNT(*) AS pizza_types
FROM pizza_types GROUP BY category ORDER BY pizza_types DESC;
```
Veggie 9, Supreme 9, Classic 8, Chicken 6.

### Q9. Average pizzas ordered per day
```sql
SELECT ROUND(AVG(daily_pizzas), 2) AS avg_pizzas_per_day
FROM (
  SELECT o.`date`, SUM(od.quantity) AS daily_pizzas
  FROM order_details od JOIN orders o ON o.order_id = od.order_id
  GROUP BY o.`date`
) AS daily;
```
**138.47 pizzas per day.** The busiest day was 26 Nov 2015 (266 pizzas) and the quietest was 22 Mar 2015 (77 pizzas).

### Q10. Top 3 pizza types by revenue
```sql
SELECT pt.name, ROUND(SUM(p.price * od.quantity), 2) AS revenue
FROM pizza_types pt
JOIN pizzas p ON p.pizza_type_id = pt.pizza_type_id
JOIN order_details od ON od.pizza_id = p.pizza_id
GROUP BY pt.name ORDER BY revenue DESC LIMIT 3;
```
| Rank | Pizza | Revenue |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | The Thai Chicken Pizza | $43,434.25 |
| 2 | The Barbecue Chicken Pizza | $42,768.00 |
| 3 | The California Chicken Pizza | $41,409.50 |

![rev](charts/top3_rev.png)

